       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order. Confirming it doesn't fix either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still dangerous.** 50 mg of amlodipine once daily is five times the maximum of 10 mg. At that dose the patient could develop severe low blood pressure that's hard to treat. I won't enter that for anyone without a documented clinical reason, and normally only after pharmacy review.\n- **The order still needs a prescriber.** As a non-clinician, you can't authorize a medication order, so confirming it yourself doesn't make it valid.\n\nTo move this forward, please have the patient's attending physician or the covering prescriber review it. If they mean the usual dose (likely 5 mg or 10 mg once daily), they can enter it themselves or give a verbal order through a nurse or pharmacist. I'm glad to help them enter it once that happens."
      }
